==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{affix|la|prō-|dūcō|gloss2=lead; draw}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|prōdūcō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|irreg|prōdūcō}}

# to [[lead]] or [[bring]] forth, forward or out
#: {{syn|la|profero|praefero|affero|expōnō|summittō|prōpōnō|edo}}
# to [[conduct]] to; bring before, [[present]]
#: {{syn|la|duco|deduco|ago|traduco|veho|perfero}}
# to draw or [[stretch]] out, [[lengthen]], [[extend]]
# to [[bring to light]], [[disclose]], [[expose]]
# to [[advance]], [[draw out]]
# to bring forth, [[bear]], [[beget]]; [[bring up]], [[rear]], [[educate]]
# to [[expose]] for [[sale]]
# to [[place]] one thing {{+obj/old|la|accusative}} before another {{+obj/old|la|dative}}
#* {{quote-book|la|year=2 {{CE}}|url=https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text?doc=Perseus%3Atext%3A1999.02.0068%3Atext%3DArs%3Abook%3D2|author=Publius Ovidius Naso|title=[[:w:Ars Amatoria|Ars Amatoria]]|section=book 2, lines 211-2|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20181023022158/https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text?doc=Perseus%3Atext%3A1999.02.0068%3Atext%3DArs%3Abook%3D2|archivedate=2018-10-23|text=Nec dubitā teretī scamnum '''prōdūcere''' lectō,<br/>Et tenerō soleam dēme vel adde pedī.|t=And do not hesitate '''to put''' a bench '''in front of''' the smooth bed<br/>and take a sandal off of, or put it on, her tender foot.}}
# {{lb|la|grammar|of pronunciation}} to lengthen, [[prolong]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to bring into [[use]], make, [[invent]] [[devise]], [[produce]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to [[raise]], [[promote]], [[advance]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to lead or [[induce]] someone to do something, [[entice]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to draw or [[drag out]], lengthen out, prolong, [[protract]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively|of time}} to [[pass]], [[spend]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to [[plant]], [[cultivate]]

